Q: Spring Boot MCP server. Specify outputSchema A: <p>this is how I could enforce an outputSchema for a simple Demo Tool. Using a String as return value doesn't seem to work, so I created a record:</p>
<pre><code>@McpTool(name = &quot;demo_message&quot;, description = &quot;Returns a static demo message to test the MCP integration.&quot;, generateOutputSchema = true)
public Mono&lt;DemoMessage&gt; getDemoMessage() {
    return Mono.just(new DemoMessage(&quot;This String was returned via MCP Tool&quot;));
}

public record DemoMessage(String demoMessage) {

}
</code></pre>
